-- title:
--   Inertia at a principal-series prime q with v_q(M)=2
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form for $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor of $M$). Let $\lambda$ and $q$ be primes with $q\ne\lambda$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, and let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with finite residue field and with $\lambda$ in its maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms of level $M$ generated by the chosen Hecke generators away from $S$) to $\mathbb C$ sending $T_\ell$ to the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, let $\iota$ map the image of $\chi_g$ into $O'$, and let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic O'`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16): an adically continuous representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on a free $O'$-module of rank $2$. Assume for every such $\ell$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field, that $\mathrm{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X+\ell$. Assume further that $g$ admits a nonzero adelic lift $\Phi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb Q$ (left invariance under global points, right invariance under the level-$M$ finite level-one subgroup, and archimedean specialisation by the weight-two slash action of $g$ at $i$), that $\mu_1,\mu_2:\mathbb{Q}_q^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$ are homomorphisms, and that there is a nonzero $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant $\mathbb C$-linear map from the adelic span of $\Phi$ to the principal-series carrier [`LocalNewvector.PSCarrier q μ₁ μ₂`](def/LocalNewvector_PrincipalSeriesCarrier.html#L173). Finally assume $v_q(M)=2$. Then there exist a local domain $O''$, an injective local ring homomorphism $j:O'\to O''$, and a function $a$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $O''^\times$ such that: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, the image under $j$ of $\mathrm{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))$ equals $(X-a(\sigma))(X-a(\sigma)^{-1})$; for each such $P$ and $\sigma$ there is a norm-one unit $u\in\mathbb{Q}_q^\times$ (a member of [`LocalNewvector.higherUnits q 0`](def/LocalNewvector_CharConductor.html#L62)) with $a(\sigma)^n=1\iff \mu_1(u)^n=1$ for all $n\in\mathbb N$; and conversely, for every norm-one unit $u$ and every such $P$ there is a $\sigma$ in that inertia subgroup with $a(\sigma)^n=1\iff \mu_1(u)^n=1$ for all $n$.
--
--   This is the $v_q(M)=2$ case of local-global compatibility at a prime $q$ of principal-series type away from the residual characteristic: after a faithfully flat enlargement of the coefficient ring, inertia at $q$ acts with eigenvalues $a(\sigma)^{\pm1}$ whose orders range exactly over the orders of the values of $\mu_1$ on the units. It feeds the analysis of the $q$-exponent of the level in the level-lowering step, being cited in the determination of principal-series versus supercuspidal behaviour and in the divisibility statements for $\lambda$ arising from unipotent residual image.
